course: dictionary
lesson: 14934
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives registrar three meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. Look at the words around it to choose the right one.
explain: «Mia's parents went to the register office, where the registrar wrote down their marriage.» Register office and marriage are the clues. This registrar is an official who keeps records.
explain: «The registrar will see you now,» said the nurse at the hospital. Hospital is the clue here. This registrar is a doctor in training, and quite senior.
explain: Use the check from earlier lessons: swap your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably chosen well.
fact: A registrar is an official who keeps records, especially of births, marriages and deaths.
fact: In the UK, a baby's birth must be registered with the registrar.
fact: Couples can be married by a registrar at a register office instead of in a church.
fact: At a school or university, the registrar is the person in charge of student records and admissions.
fact: In UK hospitals, a registrar is a doctor in training to become a consultant, which is a senior specialist.
exercise: «Dad took the form to the registrar to record my baby sister's birth.» What is a registrar in this sentence? | *An official who keeps records | A kind of bird | The person who runs the school canteen | A doctor in training
exercise: «The registrar will see you now,» said the nurse. What kind of registrar is this? | *A doctor in training, quite senior | A cook in the hospital kitchen | A teacher | A school secretary
exercise: Who is the registrar that looks after student records and admissions? | A nurse on a ward | A bus driver | A shop assistant | *The person in charge at a school or university
test: «Ellie and Tom got married at the register office, and the registrar signed the papers.» What job does the registrar do here? | Drives the bus | *Keeps official records of marriages | Runs a bakery
test: Sam's mum says, «I'm seeing the registrar about my tests at the hospital.» Which meaning fits best? | *A senior doctor in training | An official who keeps records | A teacher in charge of exams
exam: Which word is the clue that this registrar is a doctor? «The registrar will see you at the hospital.» | *hospital | you | see | registrar
